\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs24 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Incipit summula fratris Ch\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [unradi] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  de ordine fratrum minorum doctoris utriusque iuris\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8249 \'8b Verzeichnis der tituli. Prolog: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Hic opusculum in tres partes dividitur. In prima agit de decimis et voto\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ..., (75\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) Text: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  D\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8249 \'8b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  ecime ut ait decretum sunt tributa gentium animarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ...\endash ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Extra III de sententia excommunicationis cum illorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24   (X 5.39.32). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Super operis perfectionem veniam postulo a lectore Et ut oret pro me misero Chunrado ad dominum Ihesum Christum Amen. Explicit summula fratris Conradi de ordine fratrum minorum doctoris utriusque iuris tam canonici quam civilis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 .
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Kaeppeli,\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20   Scriptores, Nr. 774 (Hs. genannt); \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Bloomfield\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Incipits 2381. \endash  Ed. auf Basis dieser Hs. (Sigle Mb): Jean Pierre\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20  Renard\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Trois sommes de p\u233 \'e9nitence de la premi\u232 \'e8re moiti\u233 \'e9 du XIII\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 e\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20   si\u232 \'e8cle, Bd. 1-2, Louvain 1989, zur Verfasserfrage (Conradus Teutonicus/de Huxaria?) Bd. 1, S. 73 ff. \endash  Zum Werk: Johannes\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20  Dietterle\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Die Summae confessorum sive de casibus conscientiae, in: Zeitschrift f\u252 \'fcr Kirchengeschichte 24 (1903), S. 520-530, 26 (1905), S. 79-80. }

