\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Incipit tractatus de origine et progressu atque proprio titulo ordinis scilicet fratrum heremitarum s. Augustini per reverendissimum magistrum fratrem Heinr\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  [icum de Frimaria] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  sacre theologie et ordinis predicti professorem compilatus anno domini M\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 o\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   CCC\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 o\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   XXX\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 o\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24   quarto\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  \u8249 \'8b. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  Quia sunt nonnulli ignorantes modum conversionis et actum conversationis gloriosissimi doctoris beati Augustini singularis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24  ...\endash ... (172\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24  ut sibi a fidelibus suis digne et laudabiliter serviatur. Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24 . 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  Leicht gek\u252 \'fcrzte Version, am Ende (172\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 ) zwei kurze Zus\u228 \'e4tze von derselben Hand erg\u228 \'e4nzt: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs20  Post obitum s. Augustini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20  ..., abgedruckt in der Ed. S. 85f. \endash  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Zumkeller\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Manuskripte, Nr. 317 (Hs. genannt). \endash  Ed. (diese Hs. ber\u252 \'fccksichtigt, Sigle M): Rudolph\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20  Arbesmann\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , Henry of Friemar\rquote s Treatise on the origin and development of the Order of the Hermit Friars and its true and real title, in: Augustiniana 6 (1956), S. 37-145. \endash  Zum Werk: Eric Leland \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs20 Saak\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 , High way to heaven. The Augustinian platform between reform and Reformation 1292-1524. Leiden 2002 (Studies in medieval and Reformation thought 89), S. 209-218.}

